Bug 2033777 - Change class.com / bbcollab.com intervention to Chrome UA override; r=twisniewski,webcompat-reviewers

Blackboard Collaborate / Class.com has updated their client-side check to explicitly test for 'Firefox' in navigator.userAgent. Using 'add_Chrome' leaves the Firefox token in place, which triggers the 'Firefox not supported' block screen. Switching to 'Chrome' sets noFxQuantum=true and generates a clean Chrome User-Agent without the Firefox token.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298664

diff --git a/browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1912923-class.com.json b/browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1912923-class.com.json
--- a/browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1912923-class.com.json
+++ b/browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1912923-class.com.json
@@ -17,5 +17,5 @@
   "interventions": [
     {
       "platforms": ["all"],
-      "ua_string": ["add_Chrome"]
+      "ua_string": ["Chrome"]
     }
   ]
 }

